Subject: Cantor Succeeding SOP Fixture Rollback P0 Data Design

@ [design_uuid] 8c20da2a-980c-45e2-a328-4054a2618a90
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] c15384bd-34a6-4b75-ae54-78281c1da583

& [Commission]
  + profile commission_ref fixture_root_ref recovery_owner_ref persistence_receipt trigger failed_snapshot_ref restored_snapshot_ref evidence_refs fixture_only live_activation_allowed cleanup_authorized commission_digest
  + trigger is a closed enum with only boot_validation_failed admitted in P0
  + commission and nested upstream forms deny unknown fields and remain bounded by 16777216 UTF-8 bytes

& [RestoredState]
  + reuse the strict B2B1 registry-record profile rather than introduce a second registry grammar
  + restored snapshot has commissioned identity same registry identity current physical generation plus one predecessor revision and digest predecessor source path supplied evidence and recomputed snapshot digest
  + restored record retains fixture root activation authority recovery owner and B2A transaction while replacing only the embedded current snapshot and record digest

& [Receipt]
  + profile status authority verified checks commission current failed record restored record trigger and raw digests plus physical and nonphysical result flags
  + success status fixture_registry_rolled_back_awaiting_boot_validation and authority synthetic_fixture_recovery_only
  + rollback_executed means registry replacement and final replay succeeded; it does not mean the restored SOP booted

& [Fault]
  + typed code field message physical_contact replacement_performed owned_temp_removed failed_candidate_preserved
  + post-replacement durability failure retains replacement_performed true and cannot claim rollback success

& [DigestDomains]
  + commission restored receipt and every reused nested record retain separate canonical SHA256 domains
  + raw current predecessor-source temporary and final byte digests remain distinct from semantic form digests

& [Determinism]
  + no clock environment random identity discovery process network or provider input enters production
  + caller supplies every identity trigger evidence and explicit root; canonical bytes end in one LF
